You'll want to install Mocha and an assertion library like Chai for better testing capabilities. You can do this with:

```bash
npm install --save-dev mocha chai
```

After setting up your testing environment, you can run your tests with a command like:

```bash
npx mocha your-test-file.js
```

This setup will allow you to verify that your validation rules are functioning as expected, fostering an overall more reliable application.

If you prefer a more comprehensive testing library, you could also look into Jest, which provides a robust testing framework and is quite popular in the JavaScript community. 

